A symbolic link named like a C header that points at itself, in a directory that
holds no package. No compiler can read a link that loops, so it is no source and
names nothing: nothing is retained.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/loop

go 1.27.0
-- docs/loop.h.symlink --
loop.h
-- p/p.go --
package p

const Limit = 3

var spare int

func Run() {}
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/loop/p"

func main() { p.Run() }
